# Normalise line endings.
#
# Without this, a Windows checkout converts every text file to CRLF, and Go
# source is text. Three consequences, one of which was a red CI job:
#
#   - Tests that read a source file and look for a literal snippet containing
#     "\n" stop matching, because the file now has "\r\n". That is exactly how
#     TestPullFailureDoesNotAbortSetup failed on windows-latest while passing
#     everywhere else.
#   - gofmt disagrees with the checkout, so a Windows contributor's first
#     commit reformats every file it touches.
#   - Shell scripts and testdata fixtures with CRLF fail in ways that read as
#     logic bugs rather than encoding ones.
#
# LF in the repository, LF in the working tree, on every platform.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Except where the platform genuinely requires CRLF.
*.bat  text eol=crlf
*.cmd  text eol=crlf
*.ps1  text eol=crlf

# Binary, never touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pdf  binary
*.zip  binary
*.gz   binary
*.wav  binary
*.bin  binary
*.onnx binary
